WEBVTT

00:00:04.909 --> 00:00:07.145
I must do what I need to do.

00:00:09.481 --> 00:00:12.050
I cannot forgive anyone who threatens

00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:14.319
Mariko's happiness…

00:00:15.253 --> 00:00:17.856
I looked into you too, you know.

00:00:17.922 --> 00:00:20.758
What are you to Mariko?

00:00:21.526 --> 00:00:23.528
…because I'm the only one
by Mariko's side,

00:00:25.063 --> 00:00:25.897
protecting her.

00:00:34.139 --> 00:00:36.141
Don't just stand there. Have a seat.

00:00:37.976 --> 00:00:40.011
-I'll make us some tea.
-That's all right.

00:00:40.578 --> 00:00:42.247
Don't be like that.

00:00:43.114 --> 00:00:44.782
These are very fine tea leaves.

00:00:44.849 --> 00:00:46.651
PROFILE

00:00:46.718 --> 00:00:50.155
Your parents' home is very close to ours.

00:00:50.855 --> 00:00:55.426
3-4-8 Kita-Okamoto, Setagaya Ward, Tokyo.

00:00:56.561 --> 00:01:00.598
You're the same age as Mariko, went to
the same schools as her, even university.

00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:03.101
And to top it off,
you both joined Nose Cosmetics.

00:01:05.837 --> 00:01:09.340
So, what instructions did Mariko give you?

00:01:10.542 --> 00:01:14.412
That girl acts like she has
no interest in company politics.

00:01:14.913 --> 00:01:18.082
Yet she quietly had her childhood friend
placed right by her side.

00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:20.084
I wonder what she's planning.

00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:26.157
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:01:26.691 --> 00:01:29.827
Hearing you say "childhood friend"…

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:33.331
What? That's creepy.

00:01:37.035 --> 00:01:38.903
I heard something very interesting.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.138
COMPANY PROBLEMS
A FACE SHROUDED IN DARKNESS

00:01:40.205 --> 00:01:42.006
It seems you're currently under suspicion.

00:01:43.741 --> 00:01:45.009
Then I got it.

00:01:46.411 --> 00:01:49.247
It was also you who sent this
to my husband, right?

00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:53.685
Tateiwa truly was hopeless.

00:01:53.751 --> 00:01:54.652
Engaging in such petty misconduct.

00:01:57.155 --> 00:02:02.227
You were in the accounting department
from 2018 to 2021, right?

00:02:02.293 --> 00:02:04.829
And after that,
the IT promotion department?

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.799
I heard you were extremely competent.

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:13.404
Illegally accessing the accounting system
to retrieve data should be easy enough

00:02:13.471 --> 00:02:15.206
for someone like you, wouldn't it?

00:02:17.275 --> 00:02:20.678
Say, why don't you join my side?

00:02:22.447 --> 00:02:24.649
I would love an underling like you.

00:02:25.617 --> 00:02:29.287
You can keep pretending to be
Mariko's ally just like before,

00:02:29.787 --> 00:02:32.156
as long as you also do what I ask.

00:02:32.824 --> 00:02:34.892
-What you ask?
-Yes.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.395
That girl is an eyesore.

00:02:38.196 --> 00:02:41.432
Her mother died so easily
and gave up her position.

00:02:42.433 --> 00:02:45.069
But in that regard,
she's not like her mother at all.

00:02:47.405 --> 00:02:50.008
I'll prepare a suitable position
for you as well.

00:02:51.142 --> 00:02:53.044
Far better than staying
attached to Mariko--

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:02.320
I'm sorry.

00:03:12.864 --> 00:03:13.731
No, so…

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.669
You've completely misunderstood
the situation.

00:03:19.304 --> 00:03:22.407
I haven't been taking
any instructions from Mariko.

00:03:24.175 --> 00:03:26.811
Mariko is an upright person
with a strong sense of justice,

00:03:26.878 --> 00:03:29.180
so she would never use
underhanded methods like you.

00:03:30.381 --> 00:03:33.651
She earns what she wants
through hard work, fairly and squarely.

00:03:34.986 --> 00:03:36.754
And I also won't forgive you

00:03:37.588 --> 00:03:40.024
if you try to scheme
against Mariko any further.

00:03:42.527 --> 00:03:45.596
What? Are you saying you're doing
all this of your own will?

00:03:47.865 --> 00:03:50.401
So even Mariko doesn't know about this?

00:03:53.171 --> 00:03:55.039
About this background of yours?

00:03:57.075 --> 00:03:59.711
What is this? How creepy!

00:03:59.777 --> 00:04:02.513
-Are you her stalker or something?
-Stalker?

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.483
-Me?
-Well, of course.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.518
You're this obsessed with her.

00:04:10.822 --> 00:04:13.324
I wonder how Mariko
would feel if she found out.

00:04:17.428 --> 00:04:18.663
Do as you wish.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:23.000
My background is something
anyone can find, like you did.

00:04:24.235 --> 00:04:26.170
But I'm certain you won't tell her.

00:04:27.605 --> 00:04:30.408
After all, if your own actions
were exposed, you have far more to lose.

00:04:40.385 --> 00:04:41.586
Around every bright light,

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.556
there are always annoying bugs, swarming.

00:04:51.262 --> 00:04:53.164
YUKIMURA

00:04:53.231 --> 00:04:56.100
SOTA YUKIMURA

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.302
YUKISONO2199

00:05:00.505 --> 00:05:02.106
You do not need to know.

00:05:07.245 --> 00:05:10.882
It's fine. I know how…

00:05:14.018 --> 00:05:15.119
to protect Mariko.

00:05:24.462 --> 00:05:26.497
‎REGARDING WHAT I ASKED YOU FOR

00:05:30.835 --> 00:05:32.203
A private investigation agency?

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.071
I'm back!

00:05:34.739 --> 00:05:37.475
Were you able to restore the PC data
from Tateiwa's secondary residence?

00:05:37.542 --> 00:05:39.610
Yes, I'm checking it out right now.

00:05:41.045 --> 00:05:44.482
There's a lot of shady stuff on here.

00:05:45.149 --> 00:05:47.385
Lots of internal company data.

00:05:47.452 --> 00:05:53.591
Did he intend to prepare all this
and stage an internal coup?

00:05:54.459 --> 00:05:57.061
Which means it was probably
someone from the company.

00:05:57.128 --> 00:06:00.798
Those expense fraud documents
sent to the president

00:06:00.865 --> 00:06:02.500
also seem like the work of an insider.

00:06:03.401 --> 00:06:05.269
Can we see where it was sent from?

00:06:05.336 --> 00:06:07.338
Well, it's tough at the moment.

00:06:08.005 --> 00:06:11.542
I think it's someone
who's very well-versed in tech.

00:06:18.282 --> 00:06:21.219
Sota Yukimura would be able
to do that, right?

00:06:21.285 --> 00:06:23.287
He came from the IT department
and was quite capable.

00:06:23.354 --> 00:06:25.656
Those skills would come in handy.

00:06:26.924 --> 00:06:29.193
But we don't know the motive.

00:06:29.894 --> 00:06:34.532
First, we want to know if that DNA found
at Tateiwa's murder scene the other day

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:38.202
belongs to Yukimura.

00:06:38.903 --> 00:06:43.140
Can't we make up a reason to bring him in,
then test his DNA?

00:06:43.207 --> 00:06:44.242
That would be problematic.

00:06:45.476 --> 00:06:48.679
What reason? We found nothing else
regarding Yukimura, right?

00:06:49.747 --> 00:06:51.182
Well, yes.

00:06:52.183 --> 00:06:55.286
Even if the DNA belongs to Yukimura,

00:06:55.353 --> 00:06:57.054
he already admitted himself that he met

00:06:57.121 --> 00:06:59.423
Tateiwa at the scene
right before he was killed.

00:07:00.358 --> 00:07:03.327
In that case, it wouldn't be strange
for his DNA to be left at the scene.

00:07:03.394 --> 00:07:05.062
-But Kajiwara--
-More importantly…

00:07:05.129 --> 00:07:06.397
Oh, yes.

00:07:06.464 --> 00:07:09.634
At 1:15 p.m. the day after
the body was discovered,

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.570
this was caught on CCTV
at Tateiwa's secondary apartment.

00:07:13.204 --> 00:07:16.374
If this person deleted the data…

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.609
There's a high probability
they know something.

00:07:19.377 --> 00:07:21.112
Identify them immediately
and look into them.

00:07:21.178 --> 00:07:22.113
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

00:07:22.179 --> 00:07:24.315
-Let's go. You and you, come with me.
-Yes, sir.

00:07:24.382 --> 00:07:25.683
-We'll go to the scene first.
-Yes, sir.

00:07:44.335 --> 00:07:49.140
Lately I've had to think
about Mariko so much

00:07:49.206 --> 00:07:51.309
that my head feels like
it's about to explode.

00:07:59.083 --> 00:08:02.553
Mariko's safety and smile
matter more than anything else.

00:08:06.424 --> 00:08:07.658
And yet…

00:08:15.199 --> 00:08:17.969
Why did I end up saying something so bold?

00:08:19.337 --> 00:08:21.572
What makes you like that person so much?

00:08:22.573 --> 00:08:25.309
Her sense of justice, I suppose.

00:08:26.711 --> 00:08:28.512
She's my hero.

00:08:31.449 --> 00:08:34.685
She definitely realized
I was talking about her.

00:08:35.853 --> 00:08:39.991
How am I supposed
to face Mariko going forward?

00:08:40.825 --> 00:08:42.093
Do you like that one?

00:08:43.027 --> 00:08:44.028
It's cute, isn't it?

00:08:44.762 --> 00:08:45.596
Yes.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.165
Looking at it makes me feel at ease.

00:08:48.766 --> 00:08:49.600
Take your time.

00:08:55.339 --> 00:08:57.274
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

00:08:58.175 --> 00:09:01.278
-Good morning.
-Yukimura, I know you just got here,

00:09:01.345 --> 00:09:02.847
but check this for me.

00:09:02.913 --> 00:09:03.948
Yes.

00:09:04.548 --> 00:09:06.817
If there are no issues,
just leave it at the usual spot.

00:09:08.085 --> 00:09:09.086
Understood.

00:09:18.529 --> 00:09:19.397
Huh?

00:09:20.197 --> 00:09:22.299
She's acting as if
nothing happened at all.

00:09:25.336 --> 00:09:27.972
It really is as if nothing happened.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.474
Huh?

00:09:31.275 --> 00:09:33.711
Wait, did Mariko not realize
that I was talking about her?

00:09:35.746 --> 00:09:36.714
Wait, hold on!

00:09:36.781 --> 00:09:39.450
What is it? That's scary.

00:09:39.517 --> 00:09:40.384
A-Are you okay?

00:09:41.519 --> 00:09:43.888
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:09:48.659 --> 00:09:52.797
I've finally realized something crucial.

00:10:02.406 --> 00:10:06.911
There was no way Mariko would think
those words were directed at her.

00:10:07.912 --> 00:10:08.779
Why?

00:10:09.914 --> 00:10:13.818
Mariko believes I have had someone
I liked for a very long time.

00:10:17.021 --> 00:10:18.055
Wait, so what?

00:10:18.789 --> 00:10:21.425
I mean someone I've liked for a long time!

00:10:23.327 --> 00:10:25.463
-Ah!
-Don't "ah" me.

00:10:25.963 --> 00:10:27.898
Besides, the more seriously

00:10:27.965 --> 00:10:30.101
I talk about my feelings for this person
I've liked for a long time,

00:10:30.735 --> 00:10:33.704
the further I fall
out of Mariko's romantic consideration.

00:10:35.106 --> 00:10:37.408
Wait, why?

00:10:39.777 --> 00:10:41.946
He has someone he's liked for a long time?

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:43.714
Yes.

00:10:43.781 --> 00:10:47.551
So, I won't be pursuing him.

00:10:48.819 --> 00:10:50.888
Wait a second.

00:10:50.955 --> 00:10:53.724
Even assuming Yukimura has someone
he's liked for a long time--

00:10:53.791 --> 00:10:55.526
He does.

00:10:55.593 --> 00:10:58.329
Why do you have to stop pursuing him?

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.933
Who he likes is his business!

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.335
What about your feelings, Mariko?

00:11:06.537 --> 00:11:09.006
Besides, it's not like that person
is his girlfriend yet, right?

00:11:09.073 --> 00:11:10.908
Is there a problem with that?

00:11:14.612 --> 00:11:16.547
I don't like that kind of situation.

00:11:17.414 --> 00:11:18.249
Hm?

00:11:19.083 --> 00:11:24.889
When I date someone, I want to build
a relationship with a future in mind.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:30.828
So I don't want a one-sided,
unrequited love.

00:11:32.429 --> 00:11:36.600
I mean, falling for someone
who already likes someone else

00:11:36.667 --> 00:11:40.337
is basically hoping they
and the other person will drift apart.

00:11:46.143 --> 00:11:48.145
He's a bit unusual,
but he's a good person,

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.282
so I hope things go well for him.

00:11:54.285 --> 00:11:57.655
I could really tell how much
he likes that girl,

00:11:59.523 --> 00:12:02.092
and it felt like true love…

00:12:05.062 --> 00:12:07.698
which I thought was wonderful.

00:12:13.204 --> 00:12:16.941
No, uh, besides, I didn't
like him in the first place.

00:12:20.444 --> 00:12:22.246
This is because you ran
your mouth, Tomoya.

00:12:22.847 --> 00:12:24.014
Me?

00:12:25.049 --> 00:12:25.983
Me, huh?

00:12:28.886 --> 00:12:31.488
Still, depending on how you look at it,
this is an opportunity.

00:12:36.527 --> 00:12:37.561
I mean…

00:12:38.262 --> 00:12:40.631
You can just start talking

00:12:40.698 --> 00:12:43.901
-to her more from now on.
-You always say the exact same thing.

00:12:44.635 --> 00:12:47.271
No, I really think this is your chance.

00:12:48.239 --> 00:12:51.842
She already knows
you have someone you like,

00:12:51.909 --> 00:12:54.745
and she understands
that your feelings are serious.

00:12:54.812 --> 00:12:56.847
Then all you have to do
is tell her that it's her.

00:12:56.914 --> 00:12:59.717
-Just say it, you got it!
-There's no way I can say that.

00:13:00.351 --> 00:13:01.185
Why?

00:13:02.519 --> 00:13:05.522
There's no way I can tell her
I've liked her for a long time.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:07.391
Really?

00:13:08.259 --> 00:13:09.360
Well, that kind of thing…

00:13:11.262 --> 00:13:12.463
I guess it's creepy, huh?

00:13:38.522 --> 00:13:40.057
The progress…

00:13:41.292 --> 00:13:42.259
Yes, this.

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:48.365
It's fine, it's fine. It'll work.

00:13:48.933 --> 00:13:50.334
It'll work. It's fine.

00:14:07.418 --> 00:14:10.821
What? Even you only got an email
from Asai, President?

00:14:10.888 --> 00:14:14.291
Yes. He has never taken
time off like this before,

00:14:14.358 --> 00:14:17.161
so I got worried that something
might have happened.

00:14:22.666 --> 00:14:25.469
Notifications went out to both
the secretarial section and HR,

00:14:25.536 --> 00:14:27.871
so procedurally, there's no issue, but…

00:14:27.938 --> 00:14:28.772
Indeed.

00:14:28.839 --> 00:14:31.108
He's not answering his phone either.

00:14:32.209 --> 00:14:35.012
Given the timing,
I'm concerned about a few things.

00:14:35.679 --> 00:14:37.881
Do you mean the Tateiwa case?

00:14:37.948 --> 00:14:38.782
Yes.

00:14:38.849 --> 00:14:42.219
If he happened to get
caught up in some incident…

00:14:44.321 --> 00:14:48.792
We also have to consider the culprit
behind Mariko's kidnapping.

00:14:49.793 --> 00:14:53.864
That Hatano man has been
talking to weekly magazines.

00:14:54.465 --> 00:14:55.933
What could he be aiming for?

00:14:57.001 --> 00:14:59.303
If he were to make contact with Mariko--

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:01.338
That's what worries me as well.

00:15:02.673 --> 00:15:05.642
Please continue to look after Mariko.

00:15:05.709 --> 00:15:07.644
Report to me whenever anything comes up.

00:15:08.479 --> 00:15:09.580
Understood.

00:15:23.327 --> 00:15:25.295
Did Sota Yukimura
really have no interaction

00:15:25.362 --> 00:15:28.565
with Mariko before he
transferred departments?

00:15:29.233 --> 00:15:31.301
Yes, that appears to be the case.

00:15:31.869 --> 00:15:34.338
Is that man Mariko's stalker?

00:15:37.141 --> 00:15:38.642
He was strangely composed

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.311
and eerie.

00:15:42.746 --> 00:15:45.249
It seems likely he's hiding
other things as well.

00:15:45.983 --> 00:15:47.684
He's definitely scheming something.

00:15:47.751 --> 00:15:49.119
But more importantly,

00:15:51.055 --> 00:15:53.824
do we have any information we can use?

00:15:54.591 --> 00:15:57.027
My apologies. Nothing at the moment.

00:15:59.263 --> 00:16:01.265
You're useless.

00:16:05.135 --> 00:16:09.106
Yukimura has a weak presence
at the company,

00:16:09.706 --> 00:16:11.842
but he's a hard worker and thoughtful,

00:16:12.743 --> 00:16:15.312
so he's liked by those
who have worked with him.

00:16:18.415 --> 00:16:20.517
-And?
-I'm sorry.

00:16:20.584 --> 00:16:22.686
Ah, changing the subject,

00:16:23.287 --> 00:16:26.323
the president called in
Mariko's subordinate, Izumi,

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:28.992
and instructed her to look into Asai.

00:16:29.593 --> 00:16:31.161
It seems that the president

00:16:31.228 --> 00:16:34.164
may be hiding something with Asai--

00:16:34.231 --> 00:16:37.000
That's fine. I don't care about Asai.

00:16:38.268 --> 00:16:41.705
If you learn anything new about
Sota Yukimura, report to me immediately.

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.275
Yes. Excuse me.

00:17:10.868 --> 00:17:13.070
WHEN TO CONFESS

00:17:13.136 --> 00:17:16.440
THE TIMING TO CONFESS…

00:17:36.527 --> 00:17:37.728
I told you I didn't need any.

00:17:40.464 --> 00:17:43.834
However, since you brewed it,
I'll take it.

00:17:59.349 --> 00:18:00.284
Is this the usual one?

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:03.687
Oh, no, since it's nighttime,
I made it decaf.

00:18:05.222 --> 00:18:08.892
You're too thoughtful, anticipating
things way too far in advance,

00:18:08.959 --> 00:18:10.060
it's scary.

00:18:11.528 --> 00:18:12.663
I'm sorry.

00:18:12.729 --> 00:18:15.365
You don't need to go that far.
Just being normal is fine.

00:18:15.432 --> 00:18:16.300
Okay.

00:18:19.102 --> 00:18:21.038
Oh, but thank you.

00:18:31.682 --> 00:18:33.116
-Ah, um…
-Ah, um…

00:18:37.554 --> 00:18:39.923
-Go ahead.
-No, go ahead.

00:18:41.291 --> 00:18:44.428
Oh, uh…

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.999
-I need to ask you something.
-Yes?

00:18:51.235 --> 00:18:53.003
Where are you from, Yukimura?

00:18:55.572 --> 00:18:57.207
Tokyo.

00:18:57.975 --> 00:18:59.610
Where in Tokyo?

00:19:01.245 --> 00:19:03.947
Around Setagaya.

00:19:04.014 --> 00:19:05.282
Where in Setagaya?

00:19:11.054 --> 00:19:14.891
Around Kita-Okamoto and that area.

00:19:16.059 --> 00:19:17.361
Oh, right near my home…

00:19:18.762 --> 00:19:21.064
Your middle school and high school
were around there, too?

00:19:21.131 --> 00:19:22.432
No, back then…

00:19:27.738 --> 00:19:28.972
Yes, they were.

00:19:29.039 --> 00:19:31.808
When you were a child,
where did you go for summer festivals?

00:19:31.875 --> 00:19:34.044
-The ones nearby--
-Why are you asking all of a sudden?

00:19:34.811 --> 00:19:37.147
Oh, no reason…

00:19:39.182 --> 00:19:43.086
Did someone perhaps say something to you?

00:19:43.954 --> 00:19:46.290
Oh, no…

00:19:47.658 --> 00:19:48.659
I just…

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:50.494
Excuse me!

00:19:51.895 --> 00:19:54.231
FESTIVAL

00:19:59.469 --> 00:20:01.605
It was popular back when
I was in middle school.

00:20:01.672 --> 00:20:04.074
Once I like something,
I tend to stay attached to it forever.

00:20:04.641 --> 00:20:06.310
I still use it.

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:12.015
Guess there's no way…

00:20:14.451 --> 00:20:16.386
There couldn't be such a coincidence…

00:20:17.854 --> 00:20:19.823
-Sorry, it's nothing.
-Huh?

00:20:21.258 --> 00:20:22.526
What about you?

00:20:24.795 --> 00:20:26.630
-Ah…
-You were about to say something, right?

00:20:26.697 --> 00:20:27.698
Never mind, actually.

00:20:27.764 --> 00:20:30.400
-Never mind? What is it? I'm curious.
-No.

00:20:31.635 --> 00:20:32.469
Really, it's nothing.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:56.727
MARIKO NOSE

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:02.733
Hey, can I throw this away?

00:21:02.799 --> 00:21:05.268
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:21:06.737 --> 00:21:07.704
What? No…

00:21:08.705 --> 00:21:10.474
Why did I do something like this?

00:21:12.576 --> 00:21:14.511
Manager, you were reading
this document here earlier, right?

00:21:15.879 --> 00:21:18.048
Since it was a hassle to get sticky notes,

00:21:18.115 --> 00:21:21.651
you just wedged it in whatever, but then
you had an idea, so you left it there.

00:21:22.519 --> 00:21:25.021
Like I said, stop doing that stuff.

00:21:25.088 --> 00:21:26.189
Why am I getting scolded?

00:21:26.256 --> 00:21:28.959
Because the way you act,

00:21:29.025 --> 00:21:31.261
like you understand everything,
it is just annoying.

00:21:32.362 --> 00:21:33.764
Are you a psychic?

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:36.299
Um, with all due respect,

00:21:36.366 --> 00:21:38.969
I think anyone could figure this out.
You're usually like this, Manager.

00:21:39.035 --> 00:21:40.904
That's not true! This was just by chance.

00:21:41.905 --> 00:21:42.739
Oh.

00:21:44.508 --> 00:21:48.345
The other day, some coffee was left
in the coffee machine.

00:21:49.012 --> 00:21:50.714
You probably received a sudden phone call.

00:21:50.781 --> 00:21:53.216
There was also a time a rice ball was left

00:21:53.283 --> 00:21:55.552
in the meeting room
for several hours, you know?

00:22:01.558 --> 00:22:05.328
It just made me think about how
absorbed in your work you get.

00:22:06.897 --> 00:22:07.931
Annoying!

00:22:09.533 --> 00:22:11.768
What's with you acting
like you're the only reliable one?

00:22:17.073 --> 00:22:17.908
Huh?

00:22:20.744 --> 00:22:21.978
Wait, wait…

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:24.347
Wait…

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:31.354
You're laughing too much.

00:22:41.097 --> 00:22:42.666
I should be heading home soon.

00:22:51.675 --> 00:22:53.243
Things are fine just as they are.

00:22:56.813 --> 00:22:59.416
I couldn't imagine
being able to talk to her like this

00:22:59.483 --> 00:23:00.684
until recently.

00:23:04.254 --> 00:23:06.456
So this is fine.

00:23:09.593 --> 00:23:11.895
If I say it, I might lose everything.

00:23:15.565 --> 00:23:16.900
I prefer what I have now.

00:23:47.230 --> 00:23:48.498
Mariko.

00:23:48.565 --> 00:23:51.268
-Yes?
-Do you like amusement parks?

00:23:52.736 --> 00:23:54.571
-What? Amusement parks?
-Yes.

00:23:55.672 --> 00:23:58.942
I don't think I've been to one
since middle school.

00:23:59.576 --> 00:24:01.211
That was a really long time ago.

00:24:02.178 --> 00:24:05.782
Oh… I end up having
too much time on my hands.

00:24:06.583 --> 00:24:07.551
What do you mean?

00:24:09.986 --> 00:24:11.488
We can ride together actually.

00:24:11.555 --> 00:24:13.223
-What? We can?
-What? That's awesome.

00:24:13.290 --> 00:24:15.325
Really? Yay, yay!

00:24:15.392 --> 00:24:17.227
-Wow.
-This is crazy!

00:24:17.294 --> 00:24:19.396
-Next, please.
-Let's go, let's go.

00:24:20.330 --> 00:24:21.498
It's written right there.

00:24:21.565 --> 00:24:24.334
-Really? You can't shake it?
-Stop it.

00:24:24.401 --> 00:24:25.535
Guys, it won't shake.

00:24:25.602 --> 00:24:27.504
It's time spent
doing nothing in particular.

00:24:27.571 --> 00:24:30.407
I don't really know
what I'm supposed to enjoy…

00:24:30.473 --> 00:24:31.808
Wow…

00:24:32.676 --> 00:24:36.379
Well, it also depends
on who you go with, though.

00:24:39.649 --> 00:24:42.519
So, what about this amusement park?

00:24:42.586 --> 00:24:45.655
Well, Sara keeps saying she wants to go,

00:24:45.722 --> 00:24:48.692
but I'm unsure if we should go alone.

00:24:48.758 --> 00:24:50.493
Sure, I'll go with you.

00:24:50.560 --> 00:24:52.195
-No, it's fine.
-What, why?

00:24:52.262 --> 00:24:53.430
-I don't mind at all.
-No.

00:24:53.496 --> 00:24:55.198
I'd feel awkward.

00:24:55.265 --> 00:24:56.366
It's fine, it's fine.

00:24:59.302 --> 00:25:04.574
I mean, I wondered how a double date
with the two of us and my kid would be,

00:25:04.641 --> 00:25:06.676
-but I guess it's impossible…
-What?

00:25:06.743 --> 00:25:09.512
Is there anything else? An aquarium?

00:25:19.022 --> 00:25:22.092
‎METROPOLITAN ART CANVAS

00:25:31.401 --> 00:25:34.104
-Sorry to keep you waiting.
-No, not at all.

00:25:34.170 --> 00:25:37.007
I'm the one who invited you
so suddenly, after all.

00:25:37.707 --> 00:25:38.541
No…

00:25:39.142 --> 00:25:40.910
-Here.
-Thank you.

00:25:40.977 --> 00:25:42.078
VINCENT WALLACE

00:25:42.946 --> 00:25:43.813
This way.

00:25:49.085 --> 00:25:51.054
Are you interested in paintings and art?

00:25:51.955 --> 00:25:54.891
Yes, although I'm not
very knowledgeable about them.

00:25:54.958 --> 00:25:56.326
That's great.

00:25:57.494 --> 00:25:59.229
Do you often go see them?

00:26:01.197 --> 00:26:05.068
Since that kind of knowledge
might prove useful for work someday,

00:26:05.135 --> 00:26:07.303
I try to go whenever I have time.

00:26:08.672 --> 00:26:10.040
You're very dedicated to your work.

00:26:11.608 --> 00:26:15.145
No, uh, it's actually not a good thing.

00:26:15.945 --> 00:26:17.414
I realized it as I said it out loud.

00:26:18.615 --> 00:26:19.783
Why not?

00:26:19.849 --> 00:26:23.186
I'm consuming art based
on calculations of gain and loss.

00:26:27.424 --> 00:26:28.725
I think that's fine.

00:26:29.426 --> 00:26:31.061
Everyone has their own perspective.

00:26:37.801 --> 00:26:39.769
My mother used to say
something in the past.

00:26:41.771 --> 00:26:42.806
Your mother?

00:26:43.406 --> 00:26:44.941
My mother liked paintings.

00:26:47.577 --> 00:26:50.046
She would stare at the exact
same painting for a long time,

00:26:50.947 --> 00:26:54.017
so I once asked her why she
kept looking at only that one.

00:26:55.785 --> 00:26:56.820
And she said,

00:26:58.288 --> 00:27:01.257
"For some reason,
my heart is drawn to this.

00:27:02.425 --> 00:27:06.129
I feel like I really love it."

00:27:08.498 --> 00:27:11.835
I want to have that kind of feeling too.

00:27:13.937 --> 00:27:15.772
It doesn't matter
if I don't understand why.

00:27:16.406 --> 00:27:18.274
Just that my heart is drawn to it.

00:27:22.512 --> 00:27:24.614
It's interesting talking to you, Mariko.

00:27:25.949 --> 00:27:28.251
You hold values
that are different from mine.

00:27:34.023 --> 00:27:36.993
Do you go to art museums often, Sakura?

00:27:37.927 --> 00:27:38.928
Yes.

00:27:40.463 --> 00:27:44.768
I actually used to want
to become a painter.

00:27:45.468 --> 00:27:47.670
-Is that so!
-Yes.

00:27:51.374 --> 00:27:52.809
Since my family is in the police,

00:27:54.010 --> 00:27:56.846
everyone assumed
I'd become a police officer.

00:27:59.849 --> 00:28:03.620
Maybe I was just being rebellious,
thinking back on it now.

00:28:06.856 --> 00:28:08.258
Did you actually paint?

00:28:09.325 --> 00:28:10.160
Well…

00:28:12.162 --> 00:28:14.664
I painted portraits of the person I liked.

00:28:18.401 --> 00:28:19.302
It's embarrassing, isn't it?

00:28:20.203 --> 00:28:21.104
Man…

00:28:23.339 --> 00:28:24.507
It's lovely.

00:28:26.476 --> 00:28:29.579
Where did you learn to paint?

00:28:29.646 --> 00:28:31.447
No, my parents were strict…

00:28:35.218 --> 00:28:37.620
There are people in this world
who have no dirt on them.

00:28:39.189 --> 00:28:41.858
‎TAISUKE SAKURA

00:28:49.666 --> 00:28:52.235
I don't like the fact that
he's keeping tabs on me, but…

00:28:56.172 --> 00:28:58.274
if Mariko can be happy,

00:28:59.676 --> 00:29:01.077
that's all that matters.

00:29:07.350 --> 00:29:09.919
Is there perhaps someone else?

00:29:12.956 --> 00:29:16.960
Someone else you're interested in
or someone you're close with?

00:29:21.464 --> 00:29:22.932
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:29:22.999 --> 00:29:24.534
I've asked something strange.

00:29:25.501 --> 00:29:26.970
No, not at all.

00:29:35.745 --> 00:29:37.513
If Mariko is happy,

00:29:38.414 --> 00:29:39.883
that's all that matters.

00:30:05.375 --> 00:30:07.543
Sakura? Is something wrong?

00:30:08.912 --> 00:30:10.246
Oh, no.

00:30:10.813 --> 00:30:11.848
Let's go.

00:30:33.336 --> 00:30:35.138
-Here you are.
-Thank you very much.

00:30:35.204 --> 00:30:36.439
-Thank you.
-Thank you very much.

00:30:40.576 --> 00:30:41.511
Thank you.

00:30:51.521 --> 00:30:56.926
There are people other than me
who can protect Mariko.

00:31:00.930 --> 00:31:02.799
-Unrequited love?
-Right.

00:31:02.865 --> 00:31:05.368
If someone had held
an unrequited crush for you

00:31:05.435 --> 00:31:07.570
for a very long time,
Izumi, how would you feel?

00:31:08.271 --> 00:31:10.006
What's this all of a sudden?

00:31:10.073 --> 00:31:14.510
Ah, an acquaintance asked me
for advice about a problem.

00:31:15.812 --> 00:31:18.147
I think I'd be glad.

00:31:18.214 --> 00:31:21.784
It sounds like a shojo manga.
"I've always loved you, all along."

00:31:21.851 --> 00:31:23.953
It's quite heart-fluttering. Right, Sara?

00:31:24.020 --> 00:31:25.989
Yes, heart-fluttering.

00:31:26.055 --> 00:31:26.923
Heart-fluttering.

00:31:26.990 --> 00:31:29.592
Right! Girls definitely
think that way, don't they?

00:31:29.659 --> 00:31:30.893
It depends on the person.

00:31:30.960 --> 00:31:33.363
It's not like all girls think
the exact same way.

00:31:33.429 --> 00:31:35.131
Tomoya got scolded.

00:31:35.898 --> 00:31:38.234
Hey, that was not
getting scolded just now.

00:31:40.470 --> 00:31:41.371
All right, done!

00:31:41.437 --> 00:31:43.573
Mama, can I ride now?

00:31:43.639 --> 00:31:45.241
Sure, be careful.

00:31:45.308 --> 00:31:46.542
-Okay!
-Okay.

00:31:46.609 --> 00:31:47.543
See you.

00:31:49.212 --> 00:31:50.246
Be careful.

00:31:54.117 --> 00:31:55.618
Still, you know,

00:31:56.386 --> 00:31:59.522
that's assuming those feelings
remain pure, right?

00:32:01.657 --> 00:32:03.026
That unrequited love you mentioned.

00:32:04.961 --> 00:32:08.798
Love is always pure
at the beginning, isn't it?

00:32:09.932 --> 00:32:13.870
Just being able to see their face
from afar brings happiness.

00:32:13.936 --> 00:32:16.906
Just sharing the same space
brings happiness.

00:32:18.041 --> 00:32:22.011
But eventually, you inevitably start
wanting something in return.

00:32:23.312 --> 00:32:25.648
When you can't get it,

00:32:25.715 --> 00:32:27.950
yet you can't pull away
from the other person,

00:32:28.584 --> 00:32:31.587
wouldn't it feel like
it's become an obsession?

00:32:33.723 --> 00:32:35.058
-An obsession…
-Yes.

00:32:36.926 --> 00:32:40.329
But what about a guy
who's stayed in love forever

00:32:41.531 --> 00:32:42.832
without asking for anything

00:32:43.599 --> 00:32:46.836
and simply wishes for her happiness,
even if it remains unrequited?

00:32:46.903 --> 00:32:49.338
It might not be impossible.

00:32:49.939 --> 00:32:51.941
But it's not likely, isn't it?

00:32:53.342 --> 00:32:55.311
Hey, who is this about?

00:32:57.013 --> 00:32:58.848
Hey, welcome.

00:32:58.915 --> 00:33:01.851
-I want to go play.
-You're playing right now.

00:33:01.918 --> 00:33:05.254
She's been saying she wants to go
to an amusement park for a while now.

00:33:05.321 --> 00:33:06.789
Should we go together?

00:33:06.856 --> 00:33:08.758
What, seriously? Are you sure?

00:33:08.825 --> 00:33:10.793
I want to go to an amusement park too.

00:33:10.860 --> 00:33:13.296
Once you become an adult,
you don't get the chance to go.

00:33:14.030 --> 00:33:14.897
Want to go to the amusement park together?

00:33:14.964 --> 00:33:16.065
-Let's go!
-Yes.

00:33:16.132 --> 00:33:18.167
Really? Thank you!

00:33:18.234 --> 00:33:20.870
Should we practice
riding roller coasters, then?

00:33:20.937 --> 00:33:22.305
-Yes!
-Yes, let's do it.

00:33:22.371 --> 00:33:23.906
What is this, a squid?

00:33:23.973 --> 00:33:25.708
-Yes!
-Where is this from?

00:33:25.775 --> 00:33:26.609
Here?

00:33:26.676 --> 00:33:28.244
This is scary, you know.

00:33:35.952 --> 00:33:37.687
Wait, wait, break!

00:33:39.055 --> 00:33:40.523
-It's okay if I use this?
-Yes.

00:33:41.057 --> 00:33:43.426
I'll wash it
and give it back to you, then.

00:33:49.065 --> 00:33:50.466
-Hey.
-Huh?

00:33:51.400 --> 00:33:53.469
Why don't we try dating?

00:33:56.005 --> 00:33:57.940
I think it sounds good. What do you think?

00:34:02.645 --> 00:34:05.882
Mama, Tomoya!

00:34:05.948 --> 00:34:07.016
Hi!

00:34:19.862 --> 00:34:21.797
MARIKO

00:34:24.800 --> 00:34:28.738
I WENT TO AN ART MUSEUM TODAY

00:34:46.055 --> 00:34:49.192
Mariko, is now a good time
to discuss the marketing slogan?

00:34:49.258 --> 00:34:50.092
Yes.

00:34:50.660 --> 00:34:53.129
I've thought of a few…

00:34:53.196 --> 00:34:55.064
Don't you know?

00:34:56.599 --> 00:35:00.836
Mariko seems serious
about getting married.

00:35:02.605 --> 00:35:05.942
-At this rate--
-She always gets what she wants.

00:35:08.578 --> 00:35:10.513
So you do understand!

00:35:15.851 --> 00:35:17.220
-Try it like this.
-Okay.

00:35:17.920 --> 00:35:19.488
-Now enter.
-Okay.

00:35:20.022 --> 00:35:22.158
SEARCHING

00:35:22.758 --> 00:35:24.026
Wow, seriously!

00:35:24.093 --> 00:35:26.529
AI is searching the data for me.

00:35:26.596 --> 00:35:27.964
It's been updated so much.

00:35:28.030 --> 00:35:29.932
Right? It's great.

00:35:31.067 --> 00:35:31.901
Mariko!

00:35:32.602 --> 00:35:34.070
Thank you so much.

00:35:36.339 --> 00:35:40.476
The system getting updated
was thanks to you, wasn't it, Mariko?

00:35:41.377 --> 00:35:42.878
Huh? Why?

00:35:42.945 --> 00:35:44.847
We heard it from Yukimura.

00:35:44.914 --> 00:35:47.617
He said you made a suggestion
to the company.

00:35:48.117 --> 00:35:52.622
You said we should get the latest AI
to reduce the burden on employees, right?

00:35:53.456 --> 00:35:58.361
Besides that, there are so many things
you've been quietly doing for us

00:35:58.427 --> 00:36:02.331
that we didn't realize
until Yukimura told us.

00:36:02.999 --> 00:36:05.167
The reason you have
so many enemies in the company

00:36:06.269 --> 00:36:09.572
-is because you're fighting for us.
-Wait, wait, wait!

00:36:09.639 --> 00:36:11.240
-Shut up!
-What?

00:36:12.108 --> 00:36:13.709
I'm sorry.

00:36:13.776 --> 00:36:14.844
Okay, next, here.

00:36:15.411 --> 00:36:16.379
Okay.

00:36:25.554 --> 00:36:29.725
Yukimura really understands you,
doesn't he, Mariko?

00:36:31.861 --> 00:36:34.263
Is it all right to leave things
as they are now?

00:36:35.164 --> 00:36:35.998
What?

00:36:36.065 --> 00:36:38.768
I thought he might be
one of the rare people

00:36:38.834 --> 00:36:42.171
you actually open your heart to.

00:36:44.840 --> 00:36:47.510
When you're with him, it feels right.

00:36:48.311 --> 00:36:50.846
You don't always get to meet
someone like that, you know.

00:37:21.544 --> 00:37:22.578
‎I hate this…

00:37:45.701 --> 00:37:46.669
Good morning.

00:37:48.037 --> 00:37:52.074
Um, do you have time after work today?

00:37:54.677 --> 00:37:56.278
Yes, I do.

00:37:59.648 --> 00:38:03.519
There's a place I want to go with you.

00:38:14.864 --> 00:38:16.699
Careful when I close the door.

00:38:24.039 --> 00:38:26.375
It sways quite a bit, doesn't it?

00:38:36.552 --> 00:38:39.054
Wait! Please stop that.

00:38:39.121 --> 00:38:42.425
What? I just moved in my seat a little.

00:38:47.963 --> 00:38:51.267
Hey! You definitely did that
on purpose just now!

00:38:51.934 --> 00:38:54.336
Ah, seriously, stop. This sucks.

00:38:54.403 --> 00:38:56.038
So this is the kind of person you are.

00:38:56.105 --> 00:38:58.140
You get scared way too easily.

00:38:58.207 --> 00:38:59.308
This is my first time on a Ferris wheel.

00:38:59.375 --> 00:39:01.310
I didn't know it swayed this much…

00:39:02.111 --> 00:39:02.945
Hey!

00:39:03.012 --> 00:39:04.814
Stop…

00:39:04.880 --> 00:39:06.615
I didn't do anything.

00:39:07.416 --> 00:39:08.250
What?

00:39:08.818 --> 00:39:11.787
Ah, is it okay if I switch seats?

00:39:11.854 --> 00:39:13.189
No, don't move!

00:39:13.255 --> 00:39:14.323
-What?
-Please stop.

00:39:14.390 --> 00:39:15.424
I can't do this?

00:39:16.392 --> 00:39:17.927
Where should I sit?

00:39:17.993 --> 00:39:19.795
Huh? I wonder where?

00:39:20.563 --> 00:39:24.834
I thought you were a hero of justice,
but you can be a bully too, huh?

00:39:26.769 --> 00:39:30.039
Because you're funny.

00:39:32.141 --> 00:39:33.943
Huh? It stopped?

00:39:36.078 --> 00:39:39.181
Did you moving cause
the safety mechanism to trigger?

00:39:39.248 --> 00:39:41.917
-No, it's moving little by little.
-Hey…

00:39:43.052 --> 00:39:43.886
Look.

00:39:45.888 --> 00:39:47.122
Oh, my mistake.

00:39:49.959 --> 00:39:52.761
Hey, it's so pretty!

00:39:55.331 --> 00:39:57.600
Something flashed just now! What is that?

00:39:57.666 --> 00:39:58.934
An unidentified flying object?

00:39:59.702 --> 00:40:01.537
-No way.
-No, it is a UFO, for sure!

00:40:01.604 --> 00:40:02.872
Look over there!

00:40:02.938 --> 00:40:05.174
-It's flashing. It's flashing!
-Where?

00:40:05.241 --> 00:40:06.942
-Over there!
-What?

00:40:07.009 --> 00:40:09.311
-Some strange light! You can't see it?
-I can't see it.

00:40:09.378 --> 00:40:10.312
It's right there!

00:40:10.379 --> 00:40:11.881
-Where are you pointing?
-Right there!

00:40:11.947 --> 00:40:13.015
Where?

00:40:13.616 --> 00:40:14.717
Ah…

00:40:17.119 --> 00:40:18.020
I'm sorry.

00:40:25.427 --> 00:40:27.196
A UFO, huh?

00:40:28.030 --> 00:40:29.365
You're like a kid, surprisingly.

00:40:29.431 --> 00:40:31.800
No, I'm telling you it was there.

00:40:31.867 --> 00:40:33.302
You didn't see it?

00:40:34.270 --> 00:40:35.838
I feel bad for you.

00:40:41.877 --> 00:40:43.679
Ferris wheels are fun, aren't they?

00:40:45.481 --> 00:40:47.583
It's much more fun
than the last time I came here.

00:40:52.087 --> 00:40:53.589
Thank you for today.

00:40:54.957 --> 00:40:56.926
No, I was the one who invited you.

00:40:57.459 --> 00:40:58.561
It was a dream of mine.

00:41:00.529 --> 00:41:01.664
You're exaggerating again.

00:41:02.765 --> 00:41:04.400
I've dreamt of this.

00:41:07.369 --> 00:41:08.337
What?

00:41:09.138 --> 00:41:13.142
Well, if you wanted it so badly,
you should have come sooner.

00:41:15.077 --> 00:41:16.512
Bet you wanted to be here
with a certain someone.

00:41:16.579 --> 00:41:17.746
No…

00:41:43.806 --> 00:41:46.609
YUKIMURA SOTA

00:41:54.717 --> 00:42:01.657
GRADUATED FROM FUTABASHI UNIVERSITY
WENT TO MAKA HIGH SCHOOL

00:42:03.125 --> 00:42:05.961
MARIKO NOSE - YUKIMURA SOTA

00:42:06.028 --> 00:42:10.165
GRADUATED FROM FUTABASHI UNIVERSITY
WENT TO MAKA HIGH SCHOOL

00:42:20.509 --> 00:42:22.611
Well, this is where we part ways.

00:42:23.979 --> 00:42:24.813
Yes.

00:44:01.276 --> 00:44:02.311
Mariko!

00:44:06.315 --> 00:44:07.983
What? What's up?

00:44:09.518 --> 00:44:12.020
It's you, Mariko.

00:44:15.324 --> 00:44:18.594
The person I wanted to ride
the Ferris wheel with… It's you.

00:44:21.096 --> 00:44:22.431
I…

00:44:28.237 --> 00:44:29.238
I…

00:44:31.373 --> 00:44:32.307
I've always…

00:44:58.700 --> 00:45:03.639
‎NEXT TIME

00:45:08.210 --> 00:45:09.044
